{
  "dom_id": "step-610822",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying the Second Principal Component From a Scatter Plot",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198769/assets/9c625bd3abc4fd02cf26119315911b24d06f8b31aa2977cf1571a8741ce091dd.png)\n\n   \n\nThe scatter plot for a sample of paired observations is shown above. What vectors correspond to the direction of the second principal component of the data?",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the *first principal component* of the data corresponds to the direction in which the data varies the most (the direction where we have the maximum variance).\n\nThe *second principal component* of the data corresponds to the direction perpendicular to the first principal component in which the data varies the most.\n\nIn our diagram, the direction where the variance changes the most corresponds (approximately) to the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ as shown below. So, $\\mathbf{b}$ defines the direction of the first principal component.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198769/assets/2b4539ab239ecf0e54d5e828079469b928dd9201ae5aa913db13104bf1ed1796.png)\n\n   \n\nNext, notice that in the 2D case, we have only one direction perpendicular to the first principal component. And this direction corresponds to the vector $\\mathbf{c},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198769/assets/a3d1e84cc1a20da39af058b422ea7860a11eb97c0afa59be752b0ca3ed0a14be.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{c}$ only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-610822\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"610822\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"21885\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-610822\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-10\">Identifying the Second Principal Component From a Scatter Plot</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"610822\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <div id=\"graphic-c15e6a9a2161adcf61a9f6b35330e0d6\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/c15e6a9a2161adcf61a9f6b35330e0d6\"></div>   \n\n<p>The scatter plot for a sample of paired observations is shown above. What vectors correspond to the direction of the second principal component of the data?</p>\n\n            </div>     \n\n            <div class=\"explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n\n            <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>Recall that the <em>first principal component</em> of the data corresponds to the direction in which the data varies the most (the direction where we have the maximum variance).</p>\n<p>The <em>second principal component</em> of the data corresponds to the direction perpendicular to the first principal component in which the data varies the most.</p>\n<p>In our diagram, the direction where the variance changes the most corresponds (approximately) to the vector <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.132ex\" height=\"2.509ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.671ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 918 1080.4\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\\mathbf{b},</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMAINB-62\" d=\"M32 686L123 690Q214 694 215 694H221V409Q289 450 378 450Q479 450 539 387T600 221Q600 122 535 58T358 -6H355Q272 -6 203 53L160 1L129 0H98V301Q98 362 98 435T99 525Q99 591 97 604T83 620Q69 624 42 624H29V686H32ZM227 105L232 99Q237 93 242 87T258 73T280 59T306 49T339 45Q380 45 411 66T451 131Q457 160 457 230Q457 264 456 284T448 329T430 367T396 389T343 398Q282 398 235 355L227 348V105Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMAIN-2C\" d=\"M78 35T78 60T94 103T137 121Q165 121 187 96T210 8Q210 -27 201 -60T180 -117T154 -158T130 -185T117 -194Q113 -194 104 -185T95 -172Q95 -168 106 -156T131 -126T157 -76T173 -3V9L172 8Q170 7 167 6T161 3T152 1T140 0Q113 0 96 17Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAINB-62\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E1-MJMAIN-2C\" x=\"639\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> as shown below. So, <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.485ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 639.5 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-2-Title\">\\mathbf{b}</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E2-MJMAINB-62\" d=\"M32 686L123 690Q214 694 215 694H221V409Q289 450 378 450Q479 450 539 387T600 221Q600 122 535 58T358 -6H355Q272 -6 203 53L160 1L129 0H98V301Q98 362 98 435T99 525Q99 591 97 604T83 620Q69 624 42 624H29V686H32ZM227 105L232 99Q237 93 242 87T258 73T280 59T306 49T339 45Q380 45 411 66T451 131Q457 160 457 230Q457 264 456 284T448 329T430 367T396 389T343 398Q282 398 235 355L227 348V105Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E2-MJMAINB-62\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> defines the direction of the first principal component.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-afcf62fd44044d12a87e7c669aa20e84\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/afcf62fd44044d12a87e7c669aa20e84\"></div>   \n\n<p>Next, notice that in the 2D case, we have only one direction perpendicular to the first principal component. And this direction corresponds to the vector <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.835ex\" height=\"2.009ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.671ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -576.1 790 865.1\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-3-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-3-Title\">\\mathbf{c},</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E3-MJMAINB-63\" d=\"M447 131H458Q478 131 478 117Q478 112 471 95T439 51T377 9Q330 -6 286 -6Q196 -6 135 35Q39 96 39 222Q39 324 101 384Q169 453 286 453Q359 453 411 431T464 353Q464 319 445 302T395 284Q360 284 343 305T325 353Q325 380 338 396H333Q317 398 295 398H292Q280 398 271 397T245 390T218 373T197 338T183 283Q182 275 182 231Q182 199 184 180T193 132T220 85T270 57Q289 50 317 50H326Q385 50 414 115Q419 127 423 129T447 131Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E3-MJMAIN-2C\" d=\"M78 35T78 60T94 103T137 121Q165 121 187 96T210 8Q210 -27 201 -60T180 -117T154 -158T130 -185T117 -194Q113 -194 104 -185T95 -172Q95 -168 106 -156T131 -126T157 -76T173 -3V9L172 8Q170 7 167 6T161 3T152 1T140 0Q113 0 96 17Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAINB-63\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-2C\" x=\"511\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> as shown below.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-50a19828e4365d90a8dbabb12596bdc4\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/50a19828e4365d90a8dbabb12596bdc4\"></div>  \n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"<span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.188ex\" height=\"1.676ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -576.1 511.5 721.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\\mathbf{c}</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAINB-63\" d=\"M447 131H458Q478 131 478 117Q478 112 471 95T439 51T377 9Q330 -6 286 -6Q196 -6 135 35Q39 96 39 222Q39 324 101 384Q169 453 286 453Q359 453 411 431T464 353Q464 319 445 302T395 284Q360 284 343 305T325 353Q325 380 338 396H333Q317 398 295 398H292Q280 398 271 397T245 390T218 373T197 338T183 283Q182 275 182 231Q182 199 184 180T193 132T220 85T270 57Q289 50 317 50H326Q385 50 414 115Q419 127 423 129T447 131Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMAINB-63\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> only.\" </p>\n\n            </div>           \n        </div>",
